# Before you plant

A quick check before committing a whole bed to hazel: two short questions,
each with an answer you can reveal once you have actually thought about it.
On the web this is an honest quiz — the answer stays hidden until you click
for it. In print there is no click to defer to, so the same two questions
are followed immediately by their answers instead.

:::{reveal question="Why does a single hazel tree in an otherwise hazel-free garden set no nuts at all?" answer="Hazel is wind-pollinated and self-incompatible, so it needs a second, different cultivar flowering at the same time to set fruit."}
:::

Spacing matters just as much as pollination does.

:::{reveal question="What planting distance is the usual compromise between yield per tree and yield per plot?" answer="About three metres apart: closer crowds the canopy and cuts yield per tree; further apart wastes ground the trees will not fill for years."}
:::

Two cultivars, three metres apart, and an honest answer to each question
above — that is the whole of it.
